-- NorthstarIQ — Lifecycle evidence integrity: a stage granted on evidence that
-- is no longer present
--
-- ⚠️ LATER-CREATED REPRODUCIBILITY EVIDENCE — written 2026-09-01 AFTER the
-- controlled lifecycle validation. It was NOT used during that validation and
-- is not historical evidence. It exists so the pattern can be re-checked.
--
-- THE PATTERN. Sales acceptance requires substantiating MQL evidence: the SAL
-- gate refuses the transition when MQL_Basis__c is blank, and the Flow records
-- Sales_Accepted_At__c only when it grants acceptance. A Lead therefore cannot
-- REACH SAL without MQL evidence. It can, however, hold acceptance evidence and
-- then lose the MQL evidence afterwards — the fields are ordinary writable
-- custom fields, no Status change is involved, and the gate never re-runs.
--
-- ⚠️ WHAT THIS EXPOSES IS A GOVERNANCE GAP, NOT A FLOW DEFECT. The Flow governs
-- transitions; nothing currently governs who may edit lifecycle evidence after
-- a transition has been granted. Which fields are system-owned, whether they are
-- immutable, and how a legitimate correction should work are undecided — see the
-- Evidence Ownership Policy open decision in docs/assumptions.md.
--
-- Observed 2026-09-01 during the controlled run: NIQ Fixture 03 appeared here
-- after MQL_Basis__c was deliberately cleared, and TWO NorthstarIQ controls
-- independently reported it Failed — Lifecycle Progression Integrity (the
-- governed route to SAL passes through MQL, whose evidence is absent) and Sales
-- Acceptance / SQL Integrity (acceptance recorded against an unsubstantiated
-- handoff). Historical execution evidence, not a current count.
--
-- Read-only. Safe to run against any org.

SELECT Id,
       Name,
       Company,
       Status,
       MQL_Basis__c,
       Sales_Accepted__c,
       Sales_Accepted_At__c,
       Sales_Accepted_By__c,
       Sales_Acceptance_Basis__c,
       SQL_Basis__c,
       Lifecycle_Stage_Entered__c
FROM Lead
WHERE Sales_Accepted_At__c != null
  AND MQL_Basis__c = null
ORDER BY Sales_Accepted_At__c DESC
